{
  "$schema": "../../../src/data/docs-authoring-schema.json",
  "id": "transparency-post",
  "title": "Transparency, antialiasing and post-processing",
  "group": "GPU implementation",
  "summary": "Choose transparency, antialiasing and image passes that fit the scene and its rendering requirements.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "per-pixel-linked-list-transparency",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Per-pixel linked-list transparency"
        },
        {
          "type": "tabs",
          "tabs": [
            {
              "label": "PPLL_GLOBAL",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-transparency-ppll_global"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "PPLL_LOCAL",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-transparency-ppll_local"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "PPLL OIT records fragment nodes in GPU storage with per-pixel head pointers, then resolves the collected layers in depth order. PPLL_GLOBAL and PPLL_LOCAL select supported storage/resolve strategies. Node capacity and max_layers bound the work; overflowing capacity cannot preserve arbitrary numbers of translucent layers."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Enable PPLL when intersecting translucent geometry makes ordinary blending inadequate, then verify memory usage at final resolution. It adds storage and resolve work and is not a universal replacement for opaque depth rendering."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Exact contracts: [PPLL_Method](/api-render#renderconfig), [PPLLManager](/api-render-ppll-oit#ppllmanager), [RenderConfig](/api-render#renderconfig)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "antialiasing-choices",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Antialiasing choices"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "RenderConfig separates AA_Function, AA scale and sample_count. SSAA increases render resolution before resolving; multisampling changes sample storage/coverage. They have different cost profiles. The default configuration uses SSAA, AA = 2 and sample_count = 4. Large outputs multiply the cost, so begin with a small preview and increase quality for the final capture."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Exact contracts: [AntiAliasingPass](/api-render-passes#antialiasingpass), [AA_Method](/api-render#renderconfig)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "blur-and-full-screen-shaders",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Blur and full-screen shaders"
        },
        {
          "type": "tabs",
          "tabs": [
